# x-release-please-start-version
CONTEXT
    Version: 1.0.0
    Repository: vinod-rightmo/inux

    darwin/amd64 https://github.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/releases/download/v1.0.0/ix-darwin-amd64
    darwin/arm64 https://github.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/releases/download/v1.0.0/ix-darwin-arm64
    linux/amd64 https://github.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/releases/download/v1.0.0/ix-linux-amd64
    linux/arm64 https://github.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/releases/download/v1.0.0/ix-linux-arm64
    windows/amd64 https://github.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/releases/download/v1.0.0/ix-windows-amd64.exe
AS ix_release
# x-release-please-end

DO Resolve the ix version from @options.target and repository from
    @options.repository when non-NULL, otherwise their Version and Repository
    entries in @ix_release. Select its exact URL for @platform.os and
    @platform.arch. For overrides, replace only the default version and
    repository in that URL. Return an object with version, repository, url,
    tag "v" plus version, and expected_version "ix " plus version. AS inux_package

PRINT "Step 2 of 3: Set up Inux CLI (ix)."

DO Probe only @host.ix. Match the parsed version exactly to @inux_package.version.
    Treat missing, broken, or mismatched installations as not ready. Return an
    object with path, version, and Boolean ready. AS inux

IF @inux.ready is FALSE
    DO Use verified @host.gh release download for @inux_package.repository at @inux_package.tag
        to fetch the exact asset identified by @inux_package.url and checksums.txt into
        one unique private temporary directory. Create missing temporary parents
        as needed. Require a matching checksum entry and verify only the selected
        asset against that entry, without checking undownloaded assets. Install
        at @host.ix using @install_rules and require @inux_package.expected_version.
        Return an object with path, verified version, and ready TRUE. AS inux

RUN @host.ix --help

PRINT Report the verified Inux CLI version and path from @inux.
